[{"input":"# Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\n- Identify the major hardware components of a computer.\n- Explain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n- Understand the Von Neumann architecture.\n- Explain how a processor executes instructions.\n- Understand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n- Explain why memory hierarchy exists.\n- Understand how hardware components communicate.\n- Recognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.","output":"","result":"# Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to:\n\n- Identify the major hardware components of a computer.\n- Explain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n- Understand the Von Neumann architecture.\n- Explain how a processor executes instructions.\n- Understand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n- Explain why memory hierarchy exists.\n- Understand how hardware components communicate.\n- Recognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.","resultHTML":"<h1 id=\"md-13g62dh-867-1objkgm-lecture-4-computer-hardware-and-architecture\">Lecture 4 – Computer Hardware and Architecture</h1>\n<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-867-1objkgm-learning-objectives\">Learning Objectives</h2>\n<p>At the end of this chapter, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify the major hardware components of a computer.\n</li>\n<li>Explain the roles of the CPU, memory, storage, and input/output devices.\n</li>\n<li>Understand the Von Neumann architecture.\n</li>\n<li>Explain how a processor executes instructions.\n</li>\n<li>Understand the roles of registers, cache memory, RAM, and storage.\n</li>\n<li>Explain why memory hierarchy exists.\n</li>\n<li>Understand how hardware components communicate.\n</li>\n<li>Recognize the role of GPUs and specialized processors.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"25cffe08e7d0933f79d613401b5f872bd9dfd006a9c8ee895c0075a6dcc373bc","markdown":"# College 4 – Computerhardware en architectuur\n\n## Leerdoelen\n\nAan het einde van dit hoofdstuk moeten studenten in staat zijn om:\n\n- De belangrijkste hardwarecomponenten van een computer identificeren.\n- De rollen van de CPU, het geheugen, opslag en invoer/uitvoerapparaten uitleggen.\n- De Von Neumann-architectuur begrijpen.\n- Uitleggen hoe een processor instructies uitvoert.\n- De rollen van registers, cachegeheugen, RAM en opslag begrijpen.\n- Uitleggen waarom een geheugenhierarchie bestaat.\n- Begrijpen hoe hardwarecomponenten met elkaar communiceren.\n- De rol van GPU's en gespecialiseerde processors herkennen."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"25cffe08e7d0933f79d613401b5f872bd9dfd006a9c8ee895c0075a6dcc373bc","markdown":"# Cours 4 – Matériel et architecture des ordinateurs\n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage\n\nÀ la fin de ce chapitre, les étudiants devraient être capables de :\n\n- Identifier les principaux composants matériels d'un ordinateur.\n- Expliquer les rôles du processeur (CPU), de la mémoire, du stockage et des périphériques d'entrée/sortie.\n- Comprendre l'architecture de Von Neumann.\n- Expliquer comment un processeur exécute des instructions.\n- Comprendre les rôles des registres, de la mémoire cache, de la RAM et du stockage.\n- Expliquer pourquoi il existe une hiérarchie de mémoire.\n- Comprendre comment les composants matériels communiquent.\n- Reconnaître le rôle des GPU et des processeurs spécialisés."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"25cffe08e7d0933f79d613401b5f872bd9dfd006a9c8ee895c0075a6dcc373bc","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction\n\nIn the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:\n\n- Represent data\n- Perform calculations\n- Store information\n\nUsing:\n\n- Logic gates\n- Adders\n- Flip-flops\n- Registers\n\nWe can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?\n\nModern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+\n```\n\n","output":"","result":"## Introduction\n\nIn the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:\n\n- Represent data\n- Perform calculations\n- Store information\n\nUsing:\n\n- Logic gates\n- Adders\n- Flip-flops\n- Registers\n\nWe can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?\n\nModern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+\n```\n\n","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-868-cz4ht7-introduction\">Introduction</h2>\n<p>In the previous chapter, we learned how electronic circuits can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Represent data\n</li>\n<li>Perform calculations\n</li>\n<li>Store information\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Using:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Logic gates\n</li>\n<li>Adders\n</li>\n<li>Flip-flops\n</li>\n<li>Registers\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We can now answer a larger question:  \nHow are these building blocks assembled into a complete computer?</p>\n<p>Modern computers are composed of several subsystems working together:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"79d09e25b39f47de51f8b26852a51665b29e583ac57f9b8aa8269e2d85af365d","markdown":"## Inleiding\n\nIn het vorige hoofdstuk leerden we hoe elektronische schakelingen kunnen:\n\n- Gegevens representeren\n- Berekeningen uitvoeren\n- Informatie opslaan\n\nMet behulp van:\n\n- Logische poorten\n- Adders\n- Flip-flops\n- Registers\n\nWe kunnen nu een grotere vraag beantwoorden:  \nHoe worden deze bouwstenen samengevoegd tot een volledige computer?\n\nModerne computers bestaan uit meerdere subsystemen die samenwerken:\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+\n```\n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"79d09e25b39f47de51f8b26852a51665b29e583ac57f9b8aa8269e2d85af365d","markdown":"## Introduction\n\nDans le chapitre précédent, nous avons appris comment les circuits électroniques peuvent :\n\n- Représenter des données\n- Effectuer des calculs\n- Stocker des informations\n\nEn utilisant :\n\n- Des portes logiques\n- Des additionneurs\n- Des bascules\n- Des registres\n\nNous pouvons maintenant répondre à une question plus large:  \nComment ces blocs de construction sont-ils assemblés pour former un ordinateur complet ?\n\nLes ordinateurs modernes sont composés de plusieurs sous-systèmes qui travaillent ensemble :\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n|      CPU         |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|      Memory      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n|     Storage      |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         |\n+------------------+\n| Input / Output   |\n+------------------+\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"79d09e25b39f47de51f8b26852a51665b29e583ac57f9b8aa8269e2d85af365d","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Von Neumann Architecture\n\nMost modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.\n\n### Main Components\n\nThe architecture consists of:\n\n#### Processor (CPU)\n\nExecutes instructions.\n\n#### Main Memory (RAM)\n\nStores programs and data currently being used.\n\n#### Storage\n\nStores information permanently.\n\n#### Input and Output Devices\n\nAllow interaction with the outside world.\n\n### Conceptual Diagram\n\n```text\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\n```\n\n### Fundamental Idea\n\nPrograms and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:\n\n- Fetches an instruction.\n- Executes the instruction.\n- Moves to the next instruction.\n\nThis idea forms the basis of modern computing.","output":"","result":"## The Von Neumann Architecture\n\nMost modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.\n\n### Main Components\n\nThe architecture consists of:\n\n#### Processor (CPU)\n\nExecutes instructions.\n\n#### Main Memory (RAM)\n\nStores programs and data currently being used.\n\n#### Storage\n\nStores information permanently.\n\n#### Input and Output Devices\n\nAllow interaction with the outside world.\n\n### Conceptual Diagram\n\n```text\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\n```\n\n### Fundamental Idea\n\nPrograms and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:\n\n- Fetches an instruction.\n- Executes the instruction.\n- Moves to the next instruction.\n\nThis idea forms the basis of modern computing.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-the-von-neumann-architecture\">The Von Neumann Architecture</h2>\n<p>Most modern computers follow a design proposed by mathematician John von Neumann.  \nThis design remains the basis of nearly all computers today.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-main-components\">Main Components</h3>\n<p>The architecture consists of:</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-processor-cpu\">Processor (CPU)</h4>\n<p>Executes instructions.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-main-memory-ram\">Main Memory (RAM)</h4>\n<p>Stores programs and data currently being used.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-storage\">Storage</h4>\n<p>Stores information permanently.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-input-and-output-devices\">Input and Output Devices</h4>\n<p>Allow interaction with the outside world.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-conceptual-diagram\">Conceptual Diagram</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ &lt;--&gt; +---------+ &lt;--&gt; +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ &lt;--&gt; +---------+ &lt;--&gt; +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-869-h2qcc1-fundamental-idea\">Fundamental Idea</h3>\n<p>Programs and data are stored in memory.  \nThe processor repeatedly:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fetches an instruction.\n</li>\n<li>Executes the instruction.\n</li>\n<li>Moves to the next instruction.\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This idea forms the basis of modern computing.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"82193468d13d58d68ebdb80ee64a724421b52acce35018dac6d89339f0d25edd","markdown":"## De Von Neumann-architectuur\n\nDe meeste moderne computers volgen een ontwerp voorgesteld door wiskundige John von Neumann.  \nDit ontwerp vormt nog steeds de basis van bijna alle computers vandaag de dag.\n\n### Hoofdcomponenten\n\nDe architectuur bestaat uit:\n\n#### Processor (CPU)\n\nVoert instructies uit.\n\n#### Hoofdgeheugen (RAM)\n\nSlaat programma's en gegevens op die momenteel in gebruik zijn.\n\n#### Opslag\n\nSlaat informatie permanent op.\n\n#### In- en uitvoerapparaten\n\nMaken interactie met de buitenwereld mogelijk.\n\n### Conceptueel diagram\n\n```text\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\n```\n\n### Fundamenteel idee\n\nProgramma's en gegevens worden in het geheugen opgeslagen.  \nDe processor voert herhaaldelijk het volgende uit:\n\n- Haalt een instructie op.\n- Voert de instructie uit.\n- Gaat naar de volgende instructie.\n\nDit idee vormt de basis van moderne computertechniek."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"82193468d13d58d68ebdb80ee64a724421b52acce35018dac6d89339f0d25edd","markdown":"## L'architecture de Von Neumann\n\nLa plupart des ordinateurs modernes suivent une conception proposée par le mathématicien John von Neumann.  \nCette conception reste la base de presque tous les ordinateurs d'aujourd'hui.\n\n### Principaux composants\n\nL'architecture se compose de :\n\n#### Processeur (CPU)\n\nExécute des instructions.\n\n#### Mémoire principale (RAM)\n\nStocke les programmes et les données en cours d'utilisation.\n\n#### Stockage\n\nStocke les informations de façon permanente.\n\n#### Périphériques d'entrée et de sortie\n\nPermettent l'interaction avec le monde extérieur.\n\n### Schéma conceptuel\n\n```text\n                 +---------+\n                 |  Input  |\n                 +---------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n| Storage |      | Memory  |      |   CPU    |\n+---------+ <--> +---------+ <--> +----------+\n                      |\n                      ↓\n                 +---------+\n                 | Output  |\n                 +---------+\n```\n\n### Idée fondamentale\n\nLes programmes et les données sont stockés en mémoire.  \nLe processeur effectue de façon répétée :\n\n- Récupère une instruction.\n- Exécute l'instruction.\n- Passe à l'instruction suivante.\n\nCette idée constitue la base de l'informatique moderne."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"82193468d13d58d68ebdb80ee64a724421b52acce35018dac6d89339f0d25edd","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Central Processing Unit (CPU)\n\n### What Is the CPU?\n\nCPU stands for:\n\n```text\nCentral Processing Unit\n```\n\nThe CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.\n\nIts job is to:\n\n- Execute instructions\n- Perform calculations\n- Make decisions\n- Coordinate system activity\n\n### Examples of CPU Tasks\n\nWhen you:\n\n- Open a document\n- Start a video\n- Visit a website\n- Play a game\n\nthe CPU is heavily involved.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.\n\nThe chef:\n\n- Reads orders\n- Coordinates activities\n- Makes decisions\n\nSimilarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.","output":"","result":"## The Central Processing Unit (CPU)\n\n### What Is the CPU?\n\nCPU stands for:\n\n```text\nCentral Processing Unit\n```\n\nThe CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.\n\nIts job is to:\n\n- Execute instructions\n- Perform calculations\n- Make decisions\n- Coordinate system activity\n\n### Examples of CPU Tasks\n\nWhen you:\n\n- Open a document\n- Start a video\n- Visit a website\n- Play a game\n\nthe CPU is heavily involved.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.\n\nThe chef:\n\n- Reads orders\n- Coordinates activities\n- Makes decisions\n\nSimilarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-870-qbt8b8-the-central-processing-unit-cpu\">The Central Processing Unit (CPU)</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-870-qbt8b8-what-is-the-cpu\">What Is the CPU?</h3>\n<p>CPU stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Central Processing Unit</code></pre>\n<p>The CPU is often called:  \nThe brain of the computer.</p>\n<p>Its job is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Execute instructions\n</li>\n<li>Perform calculations\n</li>\n<li>Make decisions\n</li>\n<li>Coordinate system activity\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-870-qbt8b8-examples-of-cpu-tasks\">Examples of CPU Tasks</h3>\n<p>When you:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open a document\n</li>\n<li>Start a video\n</li>\n<li>Visit a website\n</li>\n<li>Play a game\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>the CPU is heavily involved.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-870-qbt8b8-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Imagine a restaurant.  \nThe CPU acts like the head chef.</p>\n<p>The chef:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reads orders\n</li>\n<li>Coordinates activities\n</li>\n<li>Makes decisions\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Similarly, the CPU coordinates computational work.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2c4c8f923ae457a81c7b453b72e9f4465596e4086dce3a7f832e28f80143c5dc","markdown":"## De centrale verwerkingseenheid (CPU)\n\n### Wat is de CPU?\n\nCPU staat voor:\n\n```text\nCentral Processing Unit\n```\n\nDe CPU wordt vaak genoemd:  \nDe hersenen van de computer.\n\nDe taak is om:\n\n- Instructies uit te voeren\n- Berekeningen uit te voeren\n- Beslissingen te nemen\n- Systeemactiviteiten te coördineren\n\n### Voorbeelden van CPU-taken\n\nWanneer je:\n\n- Een document opent\n- Een video start\n- Een website bezoekt\n- Een spel speelt\n\nis de CPU sterk betrokken.\n\n### Analogie\n\nStel je een restaurant voor.  \nDe CPU fungeert als de chef-kok.\n\nDe chef-kok:\n\n- Leest bestellingen\n- Coördineert activiteiten\n- Neemt beslissingen\n\nEvenzo coördineert de CPU het rekenwerk."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2c4c8f923ae457a81c7b453b72e9f4465596e4086dce3a7f832e28f80143c5dc","markdown":"## L'unité centrale de traitement (CPU)\n\n### Qu'est-ce que le CPU ?\n\nCPU signifie :\n\n```text\nCentral Processing Unit\n```\n\nOn appelle souvent le CPU :  \nle cerveau de l'ordinateur.\n\nSon rôle consiste à :\n\n- Exécuter des instructions\n- Effectuer des calculs\n- Prendre des décisions\n- Coordonner l'activité du système\n\n### Exemples de tâches du CPU\n\nLorsque vous :\n\n- Ouvrez un document\n- Lancez une vidéo\n- Visitez un site web\n- Jouez à un jeu\n\nle CPU est fortement sollicité.\n\n### Analogie\n\nImaginez un restaurant.  \nLe CPU agit comme le chef de cuisine.\n\nLe chef :\n\n- Lit les commandes\n- Coordonne les activités\n- Prend des décisions\n\nDe même, le CPU coordonne le travail de calcul."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2c4c8f923ae457a81c7b453b72e9f4465596e4086dce3a7f832e28f80143c5dc","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Components Inside the CPU\n\nAlthough we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.\n\n### Registers\n\nRegisters are tiny storage locations inside the processor.\n\nThey store:\n\n- Numbers\n- Addresses\n- Intermediate results\n\nRegisters are extremely fast.\n\n#### Example\n\nSuppose the CPU performs:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nThe values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.\n\n### Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)\n\nThe ALU performs:\n\n- Addition\n- Subtraction\n- Comparisons\n- Logical operations\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\n```\n\nThe ALU is built from logic circuits.\n\n### Control Unit\n\nThe Control Unit coordinates processor activity.\n\nIts responsibilities include:\n\n- Reading instructions\n- Determining what must happen\n- Directing data movement\n\nThink of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.","output":"","result":"## Components Inside the CPU\n\nAlthough we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.\n\n### Registers\n\nRegisters are tiny storage locations inside the processor.\n\nThey store:\n\n- Numbers\n- Addresses\n- Intermediate results\n\nRegisters are extremely fast.\n\n#### Example\n\nSuppose the CPU performs:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nThe values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.\n\n### Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)\n\nThe ALU performs:\n\n- Addition\n- Subtraction\n- Comparisons\n- Logical operations\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\n```\n\nThe ALU is built from logic circuits.\n\n### Control Unit\n\nThe Control Unit coordinates processor activity.\n\nIts responsibilities include:\n\n- Reading instructions\n- Determining what must happen\n- Directing data movement\n\nThink of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-871-6j2xi7-components-inside-the-cpu\">Components Inside the CPU</h2>\n<p>Although we often think of the CPU as a single component, it contains several internal parts.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-871-6j2xi7-registers\">Registers</h3>\n<p>Registers are tiny storage locations inside the processor.</p>\n<p>They store:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Numbers\n</li>\n<li>Addresses\n</li>\n<li>Intermediate results\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Registers are extremely fast.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-871-6j2xi7-example\">Example</h4>\n<p>Suppose the CPU performs:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>5 + 3</code></pre>\n<p>The values may first be placed in registers.  \nThe result is then stored in another register.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-871-6j2xi7-arithmetic-logic-unit-alu\">Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)</h3>\n<p>The ALU performs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Addition\n</li>\n<li>Subtraction\n</li>\n<li>Comparisons\n</li>\n<li>Logical operations\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>5 + 3\n7 &gt; 5\nA AND B</code></pre>\n<p>The ALU is built from logic circuits.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-871-6j2xi7-control-unit\">Control Unit</h3>\n<p>The Control Unit coordinates processor activity.</p>\n<p>Its responsibilities include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reading instructions\n</li>\n<li>Determining what must happen\n</li>\n<li>Directing data movement\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Think of the Control Unit as the conductor of an orchestra.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fbb76ab97eb891aa777b78f702c0c9b04230f9d4799ffd7789c844bcb2736980","markdown":"## Componenten in de CPU\n\nHoewel we vaak aan de CPU denken als één component, bevat deze meerdere interne onderdelen.\n\n### Registers\n\nRegisters zijn kleine opslaglocaties in de processor.\n\nZe bewaren:\n\n- Getallen\n- Adressen\n- Tussentijdse resultaten\n\nRegisters zijn zeer snel.\n\n#### Voorbeeld\n\nStel dat de CPU uitvoert:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nDe waarden worden mogelijk eerst in registers geplaatst.  \nHet resultaat wordt vervolgens in een ander register opgeslagen.\n\n### Reken- en logische eenheid (ALU)\n\nDe ALU voert uit:\n\n- Optellen\n- Aftrekken\n- Vergelijkingen\n- Logische bewerkingen\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\n```\n\nDe ALU is opgebouwd uit logische schakelingen.\n\n### Besturingseenheid\n\nDe besturingseenheid coördineert de activiteiten van de processor.\n\nHaar taken omvatten:\n\n- Instructies lezen\n- Bepalen wat er moet gebeuren\n- Het aansturen van gegevensverplaatsing\n\nZie de besturingseenheid als de dirigent van een orkest."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fbb76ab97eb891aa777b78f702c0c9b04230f9d4799ffd7789c844bcb2736980","markdown":"## Composants à l'intérieur du processeur\n\nBien que l'on considère souvent le processeur comme un seul composant, il comporte plusieurs parties internes.\n\n### Registres\n\nLes registres sont de petits emplacements de stockage à l'intérieur du processeur.\n\nIls stockent :\n\n- Nombres\n- Adresses\n- Résultats intermédiaires\n\nLes registres sont extrêmement rapides.\n\n#### Exemple\n\nSupposons que le processeur effectue :\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nLes valeurs peuvent d'abord être placées dans des registres.  \nLe résultat est ensuite stocké dans un autre registre.\n\n### Unité arithmétique et logique (ALU)\n\nL'ALU effectue :\n\n- Addition\n- Soustraction\n- Comparaisons\n- Opérations logiques\n\nExemples :\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n7 > 5\nA AND B\n```\n\nL'ALU est construit à partir de circuits logiques.\n\n### Unité de contrôle\n\nL'unité de contrôle coordonne l'activité du processeur.\n\nParmi ses responsabilités :\n\n- Lire les instructions\n- Déterminer ce qui doit se passer\n- Diriger le déplacement des données\n\nConsidérez l'unité de contrôle comme le chef d'orchestre."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fbb76ab97eb891aa777b78f702c0c9b04230f9d4799ffd7789c844bcb2736980","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Machine Instructions\n\nThe CPU executes very simple instructions.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\n```\n\nA complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.\n\n### Example\n\nSuppose we wish to compute:\n\n```text\n2 + 3\n```\n\nThe processor may execute instructions similar to:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nEvery task ultimately reduces to basic operations.","output":"","result":"## Machine Instructions\n\nThe CPU executes very simple instructions.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\n```\n\nA complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.\n\n### Example\n\nSuppose we wish to compute:\n\n```text\n2 + 3\n```\n\nThe processor may execute instructions similar to:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nEvery task ultimately reduces to basic operations.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-872-1nmofrb-machine-instructions\">Machine Instructions</h2>\n<p>The CPU executes very simple instructions.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>LOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE</code></pre>\n<p>A complex application consists of millions or billions of such instructions.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-872-1nmofrb-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Suppose we wish to compute:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>2 + 3</code></pre>\n<p>The processor may execute instructions similar to:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>LOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT</code></pre>\n<p>Every task ultimately reduces to basic operations.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8e1bdeec727797adef2b166b09a22dc8b170ea07765b6801d890b29e722231a5","markdown":"## Machinetaal-instructies\n\nDe CPU voert zeer eenvoudige instructies uit.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n```text\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\n```\n\nEen complexe toepassing bestaat uit miljoenen of miljarden van dergelijke instructies.\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nStel dat we willen berekenen:\n\n```text\n2 + 3\n```\n\nDe processor kan instructies uitvoeren die vergelijkbaar zijn met:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nElke taak komt uiteindelijk neer op basisbewerkingen."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8e1bdeec727797adef2b166b09a22dc8b170ea07765b6801d890b29e722231a5","markdown":"## Instructions de la machine\n\nLe processeur (CPU) exécute des instructions très simples.\n\nExemples :\n\n```text\nLOAD\nADD\nSTORE\nJUMP\nCOMPARE\n```\n\nUne application complexe se compose de millions voire de milliards de telles instructions.\n\n### Exemple\n\nSupposons que nous souhaitions calculer :\n\n```text\n2 + 3\n```\n\nLe processeur peut exécuter des instructions similaires à :\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nToute tâche se ramène finalement à des opérations de base."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8e1bdeec727797adef2b166b09a22dc8b170ea07765b6801d890b29e722231a5","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle\n\nThe CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.\n\n### Step 1: Fetch\n\nRetrieve the next instruction from memory.\n\n```text\nMemory → CPU\n```\n\n### Step 2: Decode\n\nDetermine the meaning of the instruction.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nADD\n```\n\nmeans:\n\n```text\nPerform an addition.\n```\n\n### Step 3: Execute\n\nPerform the requested action.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n7 + 2 = 9\n```\n\n### Repeat\n\nThe next instruction is then processed.\n\n```text\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\n```\n\nMillions or billions of times per second.","output":"","result":"## The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle\n\nThe CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.\n\n### Step 1: Fetch\n\nRetrieve the next instruction from memory.\n\n```text\nMemory → CPU\n```\n\n### Step 2: Decode\n\nDetermine the meaning of the instruction.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nADD\n```\n\nmeans:\n\n```text\nPerform an addition.\n```\n\n### Step 3: Execute\n\nPerform the requested action.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n7 + 2 = 9\n```\n\n### Repeat\n\nThe next instruction is then processed.\n\n```text\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\n```\n\nMillions or billions of times per second.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-873-38p683-the-fetch-decode-execute-cycle\">The Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle</h2>\n<p>The CPU continuously repeats the same cycle.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-873-38p683-step-1-fetch\">Step 1: Fetch</h3>\n<p>Retrieve the next instruction from memory.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Memory → CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-873-38p683-step-2-decode\">Step 2: Decode</h3>\n<p>Determine the meaning of the instruction.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>ADD</code></pre>\n<p>means:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Perform an addition.</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-873-38p683-step-3-execute\">Step 3: Execute</h3>\n<p>Perform the requested action.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>7 + 2 = 9</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-873-38p683-repeat\">Repeat</h3>\n<p>The next instruction is then processed.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Fetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat</code></pre>\n<p>Millions or billions of times per second.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f14bd42716557cce2c4ce6852d10ba08d6269bd1df9bb8d1d54ba80242e8fc96","markdown":"## De Fetch-Decoderen-Uitvoeren-cyclus\n\nDe CPU herhaalt voortdurend dezelfde cyclus.\n\n### Stap 1: Ophalen\n\nHaal de volgende instructie uit het geheugen op.\n\n```text\nMemory → CPU\n```\n\n### Stap 2: Decoderen\n\nBepaal de betekenis van de instructie.\n\nVoorbeeld:\n\n```text\nADD\n```\n\nbetekent:\n\n```text\nPerform an addition.\n```\n\n### Stap 3: Uitvoeren\n\nVoer de gevraagde actie uit.\n\nVoorbeeld:\n\n```text\n7 + 2 = 9\n```\n\n### Herhalen\n\nVervolgens wordt de volgende instructie verwerkt.\n\n```text\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\n```\n\nMiljoenen of miljarden keren per seconde."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f14bd42716557cce2c4ce6852d10ba08d6269bd1df9bb8d1d54ba80242e8fc96","markdown":"## Le cycle Récupération-Décodage-Exécution\n\nLe processeur répète continuellement le même cycle.\n\n### Étape 1 : Récupération\n\nRécupérer l'instruction suivante dans la mémoire.\n\n```text\nMemory → CPU\n```\n\n### Étape 2 : Décodage\n\nDéterminer la signification de l'instruction.\n\nExemple :\n\n```text\nADD\n```\n\nsignifie :\n\n```text\nPerform an addition.\n```\n\n### Étape 3 : Exécution\n\nEffectuer l'action demandée.\n\nExemple :\n\n```text\n7 + 2 = 9\n```\n\n### Répéter\n\nL'instruction suivante est alors traitée.\n\n```text\nFetch\n↓\nDecode\n↓\nExecute\n↓\nRepeat\n```\n\nDes millions ou des milliards de fois par seconde."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f14bd42716557cce2c4ce6852d10ba08d6269bd1df9bb8d1d54ba80242e8fc96","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Main Memory (RAM)\n\n### What Is RAM?\n\nRAM stands for:\n\n```text\nRandom Access Memory\n```\n\nRAM stores information currently being used.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Open documents\n- Running programs\n- Web pages\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Fast\n\nThe CPU can access RAM quickly.\n\n#### Temporary\n\nRAM loses its contents when power is removed.\n\n### Analogy\n\nThink of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.","output":"","result":"## Main Memory (RAM)\n\n### What Is RAM?\n\nRAM stands for:\n\n```text\nRandom Access Memory\n```\n\nRAM stores information currently being used.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Open documents\n- Running programs\n- Web pages\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Fast\n\nThe CPU can access RAM quickly.\n\n#### Temporary\n\nRAM loses its contents when power is removed.\n\n### Analogy\n\nThink of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-main-memory-ram\">Main Memory (RAM)</h2>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-what-is-ram\">What Is RAM?</h3>\n<p>RAM stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Random Access Memory</code></pre>\n<p>RAM stores information currently being used.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open documents\n</li>\n<li>Running programs\n</li>\n<li>Web pages\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-fast\">Fast</h4>\n<p>The CPU can access RAM quickly.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-temporary\">Temporary</h4>\n<p>RAM loses its contents when power is removed.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-874-sxfhiy-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Think of RAM as a work desk.  \nInformation currently needed is placed on the desk.  \nWhen work is finished, the desk is cleared.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69d8e9ed064c6cd4459706fed52eb772948d82d07a145c34004fb468f6cd1927","markdown":"## Hoofdgeheugen (RAM)\n\n### Wat is RAM?\n\nRAM staat voor:\n\n```text\nRandom Access Memory\n```\n\nRAM slaat informatie op die momenteel wordt gebruikt.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Open documenten\n- Lopende programma's\n- Webpagina's\n\n### Kenmerken\n\n#### Snel\n\nDe CPU kan snel toegang krijgen tot RAM.\n\n#### Tijdelijk\n\nRAM verliest zijn inhoud wanneer de stroom wordt uitgeschakeld.\n\n### Analogie\n\nBeschouw RAM als een werktafel.  \nInformatie die momenteel nodig is, wordt op de tafel geplaatst.  \nWanneer het werk klaar is, wordt de tafel opgeruimd."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69d8e9ed064c6cd4459706fed52eb772948d82d07a145c34004fb468f6cd1927","markdown":"## Mémoire principale (RAM)\n\n### Qu'est-ce que la RAM ?\n\nRAM signifie :\n\n```text\nRandom Access Memory\n```\n\nLa RAM stocke les informations actuellement utilisées.\n\nExemples :\n\n- Documents ouverts\n- Programmes en cours d'exécution\n- Pages Web\n\n### Caractéristiques\n\n#### Rapide\n\nLe processeur peut accéder rapidement à la RAM.\n\n#### Temporaire\n\nLa RAM perd son contenu lorsque l'alimentation est coupée.\n\n### Analogie\n\nConsidérez la RAM comme un bureau de travail.  \nLes informations dont on a besoin en ce moment sont placées sur le bureau.  \nQuand le travail est terminé, le bureau est vidé."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"69d8e9ed064c6cd4459706fed52eb772948d82d07a145c34004fb468f6cd1927","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Secondary Storage\n\nStorage retains information permanently.\n\nExamples:\n\n- SSDs\n- Hard Disks\n- USB Drives\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Large Capacity\n\nCan store enormous amounts of information.\n\n#### Permanent\n\nData remains available when power is removed.\n\n#### Slower Than RAM\n\nStorage is much slower than main memory.\n\n### Analogy\n\nStorage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.","output":"","result":"## Secondary Storage\n\nStorage retains information permanently.\n\nExamples:\n\n- SSDs\n- Hard Disks\n- USB Drives\n\n### Characteristics\n\n#### Large Capacity\n\nCan store enormous amounts of information.\n\n#### Permanent\n\nData remains available when power is removed.\n\n#### Slower Than RAM\n\nStorage is much slower than main memory.\n\n### Analogy\n\nStorage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-secondary-storage\">Secondary Storage</h2>\n<p>Storage retains information permanently.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>SSDs\n</li>\n<li>Hard Disks\n</li>\n<li>USB Drives\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-large-capacity\">Large Capacity</h4>\n<p>Can store enormous amounts of information.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-permanent\">Permanent</h4>\n<p>Data remains available when power is removed.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-slower-than-ram\">Slower Than RAM</h4>\n<p>Storage is much slower than main memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-875-z73p7t-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Storage is like a filing cabinet.  \nInformation can be stored there indefinitely.  \nHowever, retrieving information takes longer than retrieving it from a desk.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"44130cd09100ea17b1ae9521bd305845bbc099ce0da5116870646b7747fd8e87","markdown":"## Secundaire opslag\n\nOpslag bewaart informatie permanent.\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- SSD's\n- Harde schijven\n- USB-sticks\n\n### Kenmerken\n\n#### Grote capaciteit\n\nKan enorme hoeveelheden informatie opslaan.\n\n#### Permanent\n\nGegevens blijven beschikbaar wanneer de stroom wordt uitgeschakeld.\n\n#### Langzamer dan RAM\n\nOpslag is veel trager dan het hoofdgeheugen.\n\n### Analogie\n\nOpslag is als een archiefkast.  \nInformatie kan daar voor onbepaalde tijd worden opgeslagen.  \nHet terughalen van informatie duurt echter langer dan het ophalen vanaf een bureau."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"44130cd09100ea17b1ae9521bd305845bbc099ce0da5116870646b7747fd8e87","markdown":"## Stockage secondaire\n\nLe stockage conserve l'information de façon permanente.\n\nExemples:\n\n- SSDs\n- disques durs\n- clés USB\n\n### Caractéristiques\n\n#### Grande capacité\n\nPeut stocker d'énormes quantités d'informations.\n\n#### Permanent\n\nLes données restent disponibles lorsque l'alimentation est coupée.\n\n#### Plus lent que la RAM\n\nLe stockage est beaucoup plus lent que la mémoire principale.\n\n### Analogie\n\nLe stockage est comme une armoire à dossiers.  \nLes informations peuvent y être conservées indéfiniment.  \nCependant, récupérer des informations prend plus de temps que de les récupérer depuis un bureau."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"44130cd09100ea17b1ae9521bd305845bbc099ce0da5116870646b7747fd8e87","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM\n\nA common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.\n\n### Program Startup\n\n#### Step 1\n\nLocate program on storage.\n\n```text\nSSD\n```\n\n#### Step 2\n\nCopy program into RAM.\n\n```text\nSSD → RAM\n```\n\n#### Step 3\n\nCPU executes instructions from RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM → CPU\n```\n\n### Why?\n\nRAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.","output":"","result":"## Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM\n\nA common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.\n\n### Program Startup\n\n#### Step 1\n\nLocate program on storage.\n\n```text\nSSD\n```\n\n#### Step 2\n\nCopy program into RAM.\n\n```text\nSSD → RAM\n```\n\n#### Step 3\n\nCPU executes instructions from RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM → CPU\n```\n\n### Why?\n\nRAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-why-programs-must-be-loaded-into-ram\">Why Programs Must Be Loaded Into RAM</h2>\n<p>A common misconception is that processors execute programs directly from storage.  \nThey do not.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-program-startup\">Program Startup</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-step-1\">Step 1</h4>\n<p>Locate program on storage.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>SSD</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-step-2\">Step 2</h4>\n<p>Copy program into RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>SSD → RAM</code></pre>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-step-3\">Step 3</h4>\n<p>CPU executes instructions from RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>RAM → CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-876-docfri-why\">Why?</h3>\n<p>RAM is much faster than storage.  \nWithout RAM, computers would feel extremely slow.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5b8100256a28a8e156622fc5a84bdfa0b680e1124845f6f4527bbabe339a6274","markdown":"## Waarom programma's in RAM moeten worden geladen\n\nEen veelvoorkomende misvatting is dat processors programma's rechtstreeks vanaf opslag uitvoeren.  \nDat doen ze niet.\n\n### Programma-opstart\n\n#### Stap 1\n\nZoek het programma op de opslag.\n\n```text\nSSD\n```\n\n#### Stap 2\n\nKopieer het programma naar het RAM-geheugen.\n\n```text\nSSD → RAM\n```\n\n#### Stap 3\n\nDe CPU voert instructies uit vanuit het RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM → CPU\n```\n\n### Waarom?\n\nRAM is veel sneller dan opslag.  \nZonder RAM zouden computers extreem traag aanvoelen.\n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5b8100256a28a8e156622fc5a84bdfa0b680e1124845f6f4527bbabe339a6274","markdown":"## Pourquoi les programmes doivent être chargés dans la RAM\n\nUne idée reçue courante est que les processeurs exécutent les programmes directement depuis le stockage.  Ce n'est pas le cas.\n\n### Démarrage du programme\n\n#### Étape 1\n\nLocaliser le programme sur le stockage.\n\n```text\nSSD\n```\n\n#### Étape 2\n\nCopier le programme dans la RAM.\n\n```text\nSSD → RAM\n```\n\n#### Étape 3\n\nLe processeur exécute les instructions depuis la RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM → CPU\n```\n\n### Pourquoi ?\n\nLa RAM est beaucoup plus rapide que le stockage.  Sans RAM, les ordinateurs seraient extrêmement lents."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5b8100256a28a8e156622fc5a84bdfa0b680e1124845f6f4527bbabe339a6274","language":"English"}},{"input":"## The Memory Hierarchy\n\nNot all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.\n\n### Hierarchy\n\n```text\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\n```\n\n### Characteristics\n\nAs we move downward:\n\n```text\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\n```\n\n### Visualization\n\n```text\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large\n```\n\n\n","output":"","result":"## The Memory Hierarchy\n\nNot all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.\n\n### Hierarchy\n\n```text\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\n```\n\n### Characteristics\n\nAs we move downward:\n\n```text\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\n```\n\n### Visualization\n\n```text\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large\n```\n\n\n","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-877-1w8pt8o-the-memory-hierarchy\">The Memory Hierarchy</h2>\n<p>Not all memory is equally fast.  \nComputers use multiple layers of memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-877-1w8pt8o-hierarchy\">Hierarchy</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Registers\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-877-1w8pt8o-characteristics\">Characteristics</h3>\n<p>As we move downward:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Capacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-877-1w8pt8o-visualization\">Visualization</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Fast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"beb62f41659ab2c17ca1a12f47834fa1b288316e5cfa9331036cdf39992f8e2e","markdown":"## De geheugenhiërarchie\n\nNiet al het geheugen is even snel.  Computers gebruiken meerdere lagen van geheugen.\n\n### Hiërarchie\n\n```text\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\n```\n\n### Kenmerken\n\nNaarmate we naar beneden in de hiërarchie gaan:\n\n```text\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\n```\n\n### Visualisatie\n\n```text\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large\n```\n\n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"beb62f41659ab2c17ca1a12f47834fa1b288316e5cfa9331036cdf39992f8e2e","markdown":"## La hiérarchie de la mémoire\n\nToutes les mémoires ne sont pas également rapides.  \nLes ordinateurs utilisent plusieurs niveaux de mémoire.\n\n### Hiérarchie\n\n```text\nRegisters\n↓\nCache\n↓\nRAM\n↓\nStorage\n```\n\n### Caractéristiques\n\nEn descendant :\n\n```text\nCapacity increases\nSpeed decreases\nCost decreases\n```\n\n### Visualisation\n\n```text\nFast / Small\n\nRegisters\n\nCache\n\nRAM\n\nStorage\n\nSlow / Large\n```\n\n"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"beb62f41659ab2c17ca1a12f47834fa1b288316e5cfa9331036cdf39992f8e2e","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Cache Memory\n\nCache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.\n\n### Purpose\n\nFrequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine studying.\n\n#### Desk\n\nFrequently used books.\n\n#### Bookshelf\n\nLess frequently used books.\n\n#### Library\n\nEverything else.\n\nCache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.\n\n### Why Cache Matters\n\nModern processors are much faster than RAM.\n\nWithout cache:\n\n```text\nCPU waits frequently\n```\n\nCache reduces these delays.","output":"","result":"## Cache Memory\n\nCache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.\n\n### Purpose\n\nFrequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.\n\n### Analogy\n\nImagine studying.\n\n#### Desk\n\nFrequently used books.\n\n#### Bookshelf\n\nLess frequently used books.\n\n#### Library\n\nEverything else.\n\nCache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.\n\n### Why Cache Matters\n\nModern processors are much faster than RAM.\n\nWithout cache:\n\n```text\nCPU waits frequently\n```\n\nCache reduces these delays.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-cache-memory\">Cache Memory</h2>\n<p>Cache is a small but extremely fast memory located close to the CPU.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-purpose\">Purpose</h3>\n<p>Frequently used information is kept in cache.  \nThis reduces waiting time.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-analogy\">Analogy</h3>\n<p>Imagine studying.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-desk\">Desk</h4>\n<p>Frequently used books.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-bookshelf\">Bookshelf</h4>\n<p>Less frequently used books.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-library\">Library</h4>\n<p>Everything else.</p>\n<p>Cache behaves like the desk.  \nRAM behaves like the bookshelf.  \nStorage behaves like the library.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-878-d36ea4-why-cache-matters\">Why Cache Matters</h3>\n<p>Modern processors are much faster than RAM.</p>\n<p>Without cache:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU waits frequently</code></pre>\n<p>Cache reduces these delays.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"58afbe9ba7ddc4280293be7b40cc624b3bf2aa721b6bf3ddea06821bd271430f","markdown":"## Cachegeheugen\n\nCache is een klein maar extreem snel geheugen dat dicht bij de CPU ligt.\n\n### Doel\n\nVeelgebruikte informatie wordt in de cache bewaard.  \nDit verkort de wachttijd.\n\n### Analogie\n\nStel je voor dat je studeert.\n\n#### Bureau\n\nBoeken die vaak worden gebruikt.\n\n#### Boekenkast\n\nMinder vaak gebruikte boeken.\n\n#### Bibliotheek\n\nAlles wat overblijft.\n\nCache gedraagt zich als het bureau.  \nRAM gedraagt zich als de boekenkast.  \nOpslag gedraagt zich als de bibliotheek.\n\n### Waarom cache belangrijk is\n\nModerne processors zijn veel sneller dan RAM.\n\nZonder cache:\n\n```text\nCPU waits frequently\n```\n\nCache vermindert deze vertragingen."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"58afbe9ba7ddc4280293be7b40cc624b3bf2aa721b6bf3ddea06821bd271430f","markdown":"## Mémoire cache\n\nLe cache est une mémoire de petite taille mais extrêmement rapide, située près du processeur.\n\n### But\n\nLes informations utilisées fréquemment sont conservées dans le cache.  \nCela réduit le temps d'attente.\n\n### Analogie\n\nImaginez que vous étudiez.\n\n#### Bureau\n\nLivres fréquemment utilisés.\n\n#### Étagère\n\nLivres moins fréquemment utilisés.\n\n#### Bibliothèque\n\nTout le reste.\n\nLe cache se comporte comme le bureau.  \nLa RAM se comporte comme l'étagère.  \nLe stockage se comporte comme la bibliothèque.\n\n### Pourquoi le cache est important\n\nLes processeurs modernes sont bien plus rapides que la RAM.\n\nSans cache:\n\n```text\nCPU waits frequently\n```\n\nLe cache réduit ces délais."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"58afbe9ba7ddc4280293be7b40cc624b3bf2aa721b6bf3ddea06821bd271430f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Input and Output Devices\n\nComputers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.\n\n### Input Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Keyboard\n- Mouse\n- Touchscreen\n- Microphone\n- Camera\n\nInput devices provide data to the computer.\n\n### Output Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Monitor\n- Printer\n- Speakers\n- Headphones\n\nOutput devices present results.\n\n### Example\n\nWriting a document:\n\n```text\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File\n```","output":"","result":"## Input and Output Devices\n\nComputers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.\n\n### Input Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Keyboard\n- Mouse\n- Touchscreen\n- Microphone\n- Camera\n\nInput devices provide data to the computer.\n\n### Output Devices\n\nExamples:\n\n- Monitor\n- Printer\n- Speakers\n- Headphones\n\nOutput devices present results.\n\n### Example\n\nWriting a document:\n\n```text\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File\n```","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-879-xfkha1-input-and-output-devices\">Input and Output Devices</h2>\n<p>Computers interact with the outside world through input and output devices.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-879-xfkha1-input-devices\">Input Devices</h3>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Keyboard\n</li>\n<li>Mouse\n</li>\n<li>Touchscreen\n</li>\n<li>Microphone\n</li>\n<li>Camera\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Input devices provide data to the computer.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-879-xfkha1-output-devices\">Output Devices</h3>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Monitor\n</li>\n<li>Printer\n</li>\n<li>Speakers\n</li>\n<li>Headphones\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Output devices present results.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-879-xfkha1-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Writing a document:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Keyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File</code></pre>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d62ca65854f68fb33f24562b67429976b54342a66906da321aad2858378275bd","markdown":"## Invoer- en uitvoerapparaten\n\nComputers communiceren met de buitenwereld via invoer- en uitvoerapparaten.\n\n### Invoerapparaten\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Toetsenbord\n- Muis\n- Aanraakscherm\n- Microfoon\n- Camera\n\nInvoerapparaten leveren gegevens aan de computer.\n\n### Uitvoerapparaten\n\nVoorbeelden:\n\n- Monitor\n- Printer\n- Luidsprekers\n- Koptelefoons\n\nUitvoerapparaten tonen resultaten.\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nEen document schrijven:\n\n```text\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File\n```"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d62ca65854f68fb33f24562b67429976b54342a66906da321aad2858378275bd","markdown":"## Périphériques d'entrée et de sortie\n\nLes ordinateurs interagissent avec le monde extérieur via des périphériques d'entrée et de sortie.\n\n### Périphériques d'entrée\n\nExemples :\n\n- Clavier\n- Souris\n- Écran tactile\n- Microphone\n- Caméra\n\nLes périphériques d'entrée fournissent des données à l'ordinateur.\n\n### Périphériques de sortie\n\nExemples :\n\n- Écran\n- Imprimante\n- Haut-parleurs\n- Casque\n\nLes périphériques de sortie présentent les résultats.\n\n### Exemple\n\nRédaction d'un document :\n\n```text\nKeyboard → Input\n\nCPU → Processing\n\nMonitor → Output\n\nStorage → Save File\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d62ca65854f68fb33f24562b67429976b54342a66906da321aad2858378275bd","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Communication Inside the Computer\n\nComputer components must exchange information.\n\n### Buses\n\nA bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.\n\n### Example\n\n```text\nCPU <--> RAM\n\nCPU <--> Storage\n\nCPU <--> Graphics Card\n```\n\nData travels along these connections.\n\n### Why Communication Matters\n\nEven fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.","output":"","result":"## Communication Inside the Computer\n\nComputer components must exchange information.\n\n### Buses\n\nA bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.\n\n### Example\n\n```text\nCPU <--> RAM\n\nCPU <--> Storage\n\nCPU <--> Graphics Card\n```\n\nData travels along these connections.\n\n### Why Communication Matters\n\nEven fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-880-5bm0v8-communication-inside-the-computer\">Communication Inside the Computer</h2>\n<p>Computer components must exchange information.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-880-5bm0v8-buses\">Buses</h3>\n<p>A bus is a communication pathway connecting components.  \nThink of a bus as a highway.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-880-5bm0v8-example\">Example</h3>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU &lt;--&gt; RAM\n\nCPU &lt;--&gt; Storage\n\nCPU &lt;--&gt; Graphics Card</code></pre>\n<p>Data travels along these connections.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-880-5bm0v8-why-communication-matters\">Why Communication Matters</h3>\n<p>Even fast processors become ineffective if data cannot reach them quickly.  \nPerformance depends on communication as well as computation.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9c621edf24cd315bb5f17b2b9b43f36fa6b42ffedfff9a5d37ced34b31bfe904","markdown":"## Communicatie binnen de computer\n\nComputeronderdelen moeten informatie uitwisselen.\n\n### Bussen\n\nEen bus is een communicatiepad dat componenten verbindt.  \nZie een bus als een snelweg.\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\n```text\nCPU <--> RAM\n\nCPU <--> Storage\n\nCPU <--> Graphics Card\n```\n\nGegevens reizen langs deze verbindingen.\n\n### Waarom communicatie belangrijk is\n\nZelfs snelle processors worden ineffectief als gegevens ze niet snel bereiken.  \nPrestaties hangen zowel af van communicatie als van berekening."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9c621edf24cd315bb5f17b2b9b43f36fa6b42ffedfff9a5d37ced34b31bfe904","markdown":"## Communication à l'intérieur de l'ordinateur\n\nLes composants informatiques doivent échanger des informations.\n\n### Bus\n\nUn bus est une voie de communication reliant des composants.  \nConsidérez un bus comme une autoroute.\n\n### Exemple\n\n```text\nCPU <--> RAM\n\nCPU <--> Storage\n\nCPU <--> Graphics Card\n```\n\nLes données circulent le long de ces connexions.\n\n### Pourquoi la communication est importante\n\nMême les processeurs rapides deviennent inefficaces si les données ne peuvent pas leur parvenir rapidement.  \nLes performances dépendent autant de la communication que du calcul."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"9c621edf24cd315bb5f17b2b9b43f36fa6b42ffedfff9a5d37ced34b31bfe904","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)\n\nModern computers often include a GPU.\n\nGPU stands for:\n\n```text\nGraphics Processing Unit\n```\n\n### Original Purpose\n\nGPUs were designed for:\n\n- Graphics\n- Video rendering\n- Games\n\n### Modern Uses\n\nToday GPUs are heavily used for:\n\n- Scientific computation\n- Machine learning\n- Artificial intelligence\n\n### CPU versus GPU\n\n#### CPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- General-purpose tasks\n- Decision making\n- Complex instruction flow\n\n#### GPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- Repeating the same calculation many times\n- Parallel processing\n\n### Example\n\nRendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.","output":"","result":"## Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)\n\nModern computers often include a GPU.\n\nGPU stands for:\n\n```text\nGraphics Processing Unit\n```\n\n### Original Purpose\n\nGPUs were designed for:\n\n- Graphics\n- Video rendering\n- Games\n\n### Modern Uses\n\nToday GPUs are heavily used for:\n\n- Scientific computation\n- Machine learning\n- Artificial intelligence\n\n### CPU versus GPU\n\n#### CPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- General-purpose tasks\n- Decision making\n- Complex instruction flow\n\n#### GPU\n\nExcellent at:\n\n- Repeating the same calculation many times\n- Parallel processing\n\n### Example\n\nRendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-graphics-processing-units-gpus\">Graphics Processing Units (GPUs)</h2>\n<p>Modern computers often include a GPU.</p>\n<p>GPU stands for:</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Graphics Processing Unit</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-original-purpose\">Original Purpose</h3>\n<p>GPUs were designed for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Graphics\n</li>\n<li>Video rendering\n</li>\n<li>Games\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-modern-uses\">Modern Uses</h3>\n<p>Today GPUs are heavily used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scientific computation\n</li>\n<li>Machine learning\n</li>\n<li>Artificial intelligence\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-cpu-versus-gpu\">CPU versus GPU</h3>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-cpu\">CPU</h4>\n<p>Excellent at:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>General-purpose tasks\n</li>\n<li>Decision making\n</li>\n<li>Complex instruction flow\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-gpu\">GPU</h4>\n<p>Excellent at:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Repeating the same calculation many times\n</li>\n<li>Parallel processing\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-881-8ev6el-example\">Example</h3>\n<p>Rendering millions of pixels simultaneously is ideal for a GPU.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6604830dda08cdec0ad4872929871697c85ac14c6735befd3439f82e2dc04f6a","markdown":"## Grafische verwerkingsunits (GPU's)\n\nModerne computers hebben vaak een GPU.\n\nGPU staat voor:\n\n```text\nGraphics Processing Unit\n```\n\n### Oorspronkelijk doel\n\nGPU's zijn ontworpen voor:\n\n- Grafische taken\n- Videorendering\n- Games\n\n### Moderne toepassingen\n\nTegenwoordig worden GPU's veel gebruikt voor:\n\n- Wetenschappelijke berekeningen\n- Machinaal leren\n- Kunstmatige intelligentie\n\n### CPU versus GPU\n\n#### CPU\n\nUitstekend in:\n\n- Algemene taken\n- Besluitvorming\n- Complexe instructiestromen\n\n#### GPU\n\nUitstekend in:\n\n- Herhaaldelijk dezelfde berekening uitvoeren\n- Parallelle verwerking\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nHet renderen van miljoenen pixels tegelijkertijd is ideaal voor een GPU."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6604830dda08cdec0ad4872929871697c85ac14c6735befd3439f82e2dc04f6a","markdown":"## Unités de traitement graphique (GPU)\n\nLes ordinateurs modernes intègrent souvent un GPU.\n\nGPU signifie :\n\n```text\nGraphics Processing Unit\n```\n\n### Objectif d'origine\n\nLes GPU ont été conçus pour :\n\n- Graphismes\n- Rendu vidéo\n- Jeux\n\n### Utilisations modernes\n\nAujourd'hui, les GPU sont largement utilisés pour :\n\n- Calcul scientifique\n- Apprentissage automatique\n- Intelligence artificielle\n\n### CPU contre GPU\n\n#### CPU\n\nExcellent pour :\n\n- Tâches à usage général\n- Prise de décisions\n- Flux d'instructions complexes\n\n#### GPU\n\nExcellent pour :\n\n- Exécuter de nombreuses fois le même calcul\n- Traitement parallèle\n\n### Exemple\n\nLe rendu de millions de pixels simultanément est idéal pour un GPU."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"6604830dda08cdec0ad4872929871697c85ac14c6735befd3439f82e2dc04f6a","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Specialized Processors\n\nModern systems contain many processors.\n\nExamples include:\n\n#### Network Controllers\n\nManage communications.\n\n#### Audio Processors\n\nHandle sound processing.\n\n#### AI Accelerators\n\nOptimize machine learning workloads.\n\n#### Embedded Controllers\n\nManage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.\n\n### Key Observation\n\nA modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.","output":"","result":"## Specialized Processors\n\nModern systems contain many processors.\n\nExamples include:\n\n#### Network Controllers\n\nManage communications.\n\n#### Audio Processors\n\nHandle sound processing.\n\n#### AI Accelerators\n\nOptimize machine learning workloads.\n\n#### Embedded Controllers\n\nManage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.\n\n### Key Observation\n\nA modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-specialized-processors\">Specialized Processors</h2>\n<p>Modern systems contain many processors.</p>\n<p>Examples include:</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-network-controllers\">Network Controllers</h4>\n<p>Manage communications.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-audio-processors\">Audio Processors</h4>\n<p>Handle sound processing.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-ai-accelerators\">AI Accelerators</h4>\n<p>Optimize machine learning workloads.</p>\n<h4 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-embedded-controllers\">Embedded Controllers</h4>\n<p>Manage keyboards, batteries, sensors, and displays.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-882-dq4he7-key-observation\">Key Observation</h3>\n<p>A modern computer is not one processor.  \nIt is often a collection of specialized processors cooperating together.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"94fc4d6b4d08652ee38fa3d77024fc53259ddc269a307c4cbfa09ec36549e507","markdown":"## Gespecialiseerde processors\n\nModerne systemen bevatten veel processors.\n\nVoorbeelden zijn:\n\n#### Netwerkcontrollers\n\nBeheren de communicatie.\n\n#### Audioprocessors\n\nZorgen voor geluidsverwerking.\n\n#### AI-versnellers\n\nOptimaliseren werkbelastingen voor machine learning.\n\n#### Ingebedde controllers\n\nBeheren toetsenborden, batterijen, sensoren en beeldschermen.\n\n### Belangrijke observatie\n\nEen moderne computer is niet één processor.  \nHet is vaak een verzameling gespecialiseerde processors die samenwerken."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"94fc4d6b4d08652ee38fa3d77024fc53259ddc269a307c4cbfa09ec36549e507","markdown":"## Processeurs spécialisés\n\nLes systèmes modernes contiennent de nombreux processeurs.\n\nExemples :\n\n#### Contrôleurs réseau\n\nGèrent les communications.\n\n#### Processeurs audio\n\nGèrent le traitement du son.\n\n#### Accélérateurs d'IA\n\nOptimisent les charges de travail d'apprentissage automatique.\n\n#### Contrôleurs embarqués\n\nGèrent les claviers, les batteries, les capteurs et les écrans.\n\n### Observation clé\n\nUn ordinateur moderne n'est pas un seul processeur.  C'est souvent un ensemble de processeurs spécialisés qui coopèrent."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"94fc4d6b4d08652ee38fa3d77024fc53259ddc269a307c4cbfa09ec36549e507","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Putting Everything Together\n\nSuppose you open a web browser.\n\n### Step 1\n\nBrowser stored on SSD.\n\n```text\nStorage\n```\n\n### Step 2\n\nProgram loaded into RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM\n```\n\n### Step 3\n\nCPU begins executing instructions.\n\n```text\nCPU\n```\n\n### Step 4\n\nData arrives from the Internet.\n\n```text\nNetwork Interface\n```\n\n### Step 5\n\nImages displayed on screen.\n\n```text\nGPU + Monitor\n```\n\n### Step 6\n\nSound played through speakers.\n\n```text\nAudio Hardware\n```\n\nMany hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.","output":"","result":"## Putting Everything Together\n\nSuppose you open a web browser.\n\n### Step 1\n\nBrowser stored on SSD.\n\n```text\nStorage\n```\n\n### Step 2\n\nProgram loaded into RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM\n```\n\n### Step 3\n\nCPU begins executing instructions.\n\n```text\nCPU\n```\n\n### Step 4\n\nData arrives from the Internet.\n\n```text\nNetwork Interface\n```\n\n### Step 5\n\nImages displayed on screen.\n\n```text\nGPU + Monitor\n```\n\n### Step 6\n\nSound played through speakers.\n\n```text\nAudio Hardware\n```\n\nMany hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-putting-everything-together\">Putting Everything Together</h2>\n<p>Suppose you open a web browser.</p>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-1\">Step 1</h3>\n<p>Browser stored on SSD.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Storage</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-2\">Step 2</h3>\n<p>Program loaded into RAM.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>RAM</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-3\">Step 3</h3>\n<p>CPU begins executing instructions.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>CPU</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-4\">Step 4</h3>\n<p>Data arrives from the Internet.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Network Interface</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-5\">Step 5</h3>\n<p>Images displayed on screen.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>GPU + Monitor</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"md-13g62dh-883-1evy8o-step-6\">Step 6</h3>\n<p>Sound played through speakers.</p>\n<pre class=\"markdown-code-block\"><code>Audio Hardware</code></pre>\n<p>Many hardware components cooperate to perform what appears to be a simple task.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"75220c77f12954d0a890400ef113acd059efba4c376c006dfbad230029168d3c","markdown":"## Alles samenbrengen\n\nStel dat je een webbrowser opent.\n\n### Stap 1\n\nBrowser opgeslagen op de SSD.\n\n```text\nStorage\n```\n\n### Stap 2\n\nProgramma geladen in het RAM-geheugen.\n\n```text\nRAM\n```\n\n### Stap 3\n\nCPU begint instructies uit te voeren.\n\n```text\nCPU\n```\n\n### Stap 4\n\nGegevens komen van het internet binnen.\n\n```text\nNetwork Interface\n```\n\n### Stap 5\n\nAfbeeldingen worden op het scherm weergegeven.\n\n```text\nGPU + Monitor\n```\n\n### Stap 6\n\nGeluid wordt via de luidsprekers afgespeeld.\n\n```text\nAudio Hardware\n```\n\nVeel hardwarecomponenten werken samen om wat lijkt op een eenvoudige taak uit te voeren."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"75220c77f12954d0a890400ef113acd059efba4c376c006dfbad230029168d3c","markdown":"## Rassembler le tout\n\nSupposons que vous ouvriez un navigateur web.\n\n### Étape 1\n\nLe navigateur est stocké sur le SSD.\n\n```text\nStorage\n```\n\n### Étape 2\n\nLe programme est chargé dans la RAM.\n\n```text\nRAM\n```\n\n### Étape 3\n\nLe processeur commence à exécuter des instructions.\n\n```text\nCPU\n```\n\n### Étape 4\n\nDes données arrivent depuis Internet.\n\n```text\nNetwork Interface\n```\n\n### Étape 5\n\nDes images sont affichées à l'écran.\n\n```text\nGPU + Monitor\n```\n\n### Étape 6\n\nLe son est diffusé par les haut-parleurs.\n\n```text\nAudio Hardware\n```\n\nDe nombreux composants matériels coopèrent pour accomplir ce qui semble être une tâche simple."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"75220c77f12954d0a890400ef113acd059efba4c376c006dfbad230029168d3c","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Summary\n\nIn this chapter we learned:\n\n- Most computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n- The CPU executes instructions.\n- Registers provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n- The ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n- The Control Unit coordinates execution.\n- Programs are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- RAM stores currently active programs and data.\n- Storage retains information permanently.\n- Memory is organized as a hierarchy.\n- Cache improves performance.\n- Input and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n- Buses allow components to communicate.\n- GPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.","output":"","result":"## Summary\n\nIn this chapter we learned:\n\n- Most computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n- The CPU executes instructions.\n- Registers provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n- The ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n- The Control Unit coordinates execution.\n- Programs are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- RAM stores currently active programs and data.\n- Storage retains information permanently.\n- Memory is organized as a hierarchy.\n- Cache improves performance.\n- Input and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n- Buses allow components to communicate.\n- GPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-884-368n9i-summary\">Summary</h2>\n<p>In this chapter we learned:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Most computers follow the Von Neumann architecture.\n</li>\n<li>The CPU executes instructions.\n</li>\n<li>Registers provide the fastest storage inside the processor.\n</li>\n<li>The ALU performs arithmetic and logical operations.\n</li>\n<li>The Control Unit coordinates execution.\n</li>\n<li>Programs are executed using the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n</li>\n<li>RAM stores currently active programs and data.\n</li>\n<li>Storage retains information permanently.\n</li>\n<li>Memory is organized as a hierarchy.\n</li>\n<li>Cache improves performance.\n</li>\n<li>Input and output devices connect computers with their environment.\n</li>\n<li>Buses allow components to communicate.\n</li>\n<li>GPUs and specialized processors perform specific tasks efficiently.\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d70d7e6e200846f58aa4018e3b5c3cfed3c0ca1a9304259303f77bc6a072b97d","markdown":"## Samenvatting\n\nIn dit hoofdstuk hebben we geleerd:\n\n- De meeste computers volgen de Von Neumann-architectuur.\n- De CPU voert instructies uit.\n- Registers bieden de snelste opslag binnen de processor.\n- De ALU voert rekenkundige en logische bewerkingen uit.\n- De besturingseenheid coördineert de uitvoering.\n- Programma's worden uitgevoerd met behulp van de haal-decodeer-uitvoeringscyclus.\n- RAM slaat momenteel actieve programma's en gegevens op.\n- Opslag bewaart informatie permanent.\n- Geheugen is georganiseerd als een hiërarchie.\n- Cache verbetert de prestaties.\n- In- en uitvoerapparaten verbinden computers met hun omgeving.\n- Bussen laten componenten met elkaar communiceren.\n- GPU's en gespecialiseerde processors voeren specifieke taken efficiënt uit."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d70d7e6e200846f58aa4018e3b5c3cfed3c0ca1a9304259303f77bc6a072b97d","markdown":"## Résumé\n\nDans ce chapitre, nous avons appris :\n\n- La plupart des ordinateurs suivent l'architecture de von Neumann.\n- L'unité centrale (CPU) exécute les instructions.\n- Les registres fournissent le stockage le plus rapide à l'intérieur du processeur.\n- L'UAL (unité arithmétique et logique) effectue des opérations arithmétiques et logiques.\n- L'unité de contrôle coordonne l'exécution.\n- Les programmes sont exécutés via le cycle fetch-décodage-exécution.\n- La RAM stocke les programmes et données actuellement actifs.\n- Le stockage conserve l'information de façon permanente.\n- La mémoire est organisée en une hiérarchie.\n- Le cache améliore les performances.\n- Les périphériques d'entrée et de sortie connectent les ordinateurs à leur environnement.\n- Les bus permettent aux composants de communiquer.\n- Les GPU et processeurs spécialisés accomplissent efficacement des tâches spécifiques."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d70d7e6e200846f58aa4018e3b5c3cfed3c0ca1a9304259303f77bc6a072b97d","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term                       | Definition                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Von Neumann Architecture   | Classical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storage |\n| CPU                        | Central Processing Unit                                      |\n| Register                   | Small high-speed storage location inside the CPU             |\n| ALU                        | Arithmetic Logic Unit                                        |\n| Control Unit               | CPU component that coordinates execution                     |\n| Machine Instruction        | Basic command executed by the CPU                            |\n| Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle | Repeating process used to execute instructions               |\n| RAM                        | Random Access Memory                                         |\n| Cache                      | Small, fast memory located near the CPU                      |\n| Storage                    | Permanent data retention                                     |\n| Bus                        | Communication pathway between components                     |\n| GPU                        | Graphics Processing Unit                                     |\n| Memory Hierarchy           | Organization of memory by speed and capacity                 |","output":"","result":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term                       | Definition                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Von Neumann Architecture   | Classical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storage |\n| CPU                        | Central Processing Unit                                      |\n| Register                   | Small high-speed storage location inside the CPU             |\n| ALU                        | Arithmetic Logic Unit                                        |\n| Control Unit               | CPU component that coordinates execution                     |\n| Machine Instruction        | Basic command executed by the CPU                            |\n| Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle | Repeating process used to execute instructions               |\n| RAM                        | Random Access Memory                                         |\n| Cache                      | Small, fast memory located near the CPU                      |\n| Storage                    | Permanent data retention                                     |\n| Bus                        | Communication pathway between components                     |\n| GPU                        | Graphics Processing Unit                                     |\n| Memory Hierarchy           | Organization of memory by speed and capacity                 |","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-885-5em0gy-key-terms\">Key Terms</h2>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Von Neumann Architecture</td><td>Classical computer architecture with processor, memory, and storage</td></tr><tr><td>CPU</td><td>Central Processing Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Register</td><td>Small high-speed storage location inside the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>ALU</td><td>Arithmetic Logic Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Control Unit</td><td>CPU component that coordinates execution</td></tr><tr><td>Machine Instruction</td><td>Basic command executed by the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>Fetch-Decode-Execute Cycle</td><td>Repeating process used to execute instructions</td></tr><tr><td>RAM</td><td>Random Access Memory</td></tr><tr><td>Cache</td><td>Small, fast memory located near the CPU</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>Permanent data retention</td></tr><tr><td>Bus</td><td>Communication pathway between components</td></tr><tr><td>GPU</td><td>Graphics Processing Unit</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Hierarchy</td><td>Organization of memory by speed and capacity</td></tr></tbody></table>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ee59aabfa36af75bbbb616e4f140e53f990db0ea162b4bf86b14a788810de47f","markdown":"## Belangrijke termen\n\n| Term                       | Definitie                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Von Neumann-architectuur   | Klassieke computerarchitectuur met processor, geheugen en opslag |\n| CPU                        | Centrale verwerkingseenheid                                  |\n| Register                   | Kleine, snelle opslaglocatie binnen de CPU                   |\n| ALU                        | Aritmetisch-logische eenheid                                 |\n| Besturingseenheid          | CPU-component die de uitvoering coördineert                  |\n| Machine-instructie         | Basale opdracht die door de CPU wordt uitgevoerd             |\n| Ophalen-decoderen-uitvoeren-cyclus | Herhalend proces dat wordt gebruikt om instructies uit te voeren |\n| RAM                        | Werkgeheugen (RAM)                                           |\n| Cache                      | Kleine, snelle geheugenlaag nabij de CPU                     |\n| Opslag                     | Permanente gegevensopslag                                    |\n| Bus                        | Communicatiepad tussen componenten                           |\n| GPU                        | Grafische verwerkingseenheid                                 |\n| Geheugenhiërarchie         | Organisatie van geheugen naar snelheid en capaciteit         |"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ee59aabfa36af75bbbb616e4f140e53f990db0ea162b4bf86b14a788810de47f","markdown":"## Termes clés\n\n| Terme                       | Définition                                                   |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Architecture de von Neumann | Architecture informatique classique avec processeur, mémoire et stockage |\n| CPU                        | Unité centrale de traitement                                 |\n| Registre                   | Petit emplacement de stockage à haute vitesse à l'intérieur du processeur |\n| ALU                        | Unité arithmétique et logique                                |\n| Unité de contrôle          | Composant du processeur qui coordonne l'exécution            |\n| Instruction machine        | Instruction de base exécutée par le processeur               |\n| Cycle Récupérer-Décoder-Exécuter | Processus répétitif utilisé pour exécuter les instructions               |\n| RAM                        | Mémoire vive (RAM)                                           |\n| Cache                      | Petite mémoire rapide située près du processeur              |\n| Stockage                   | Stockage permanent des données                               |\n| Bus                        | Voie de communication entre les composants                   |\n| GPU                        | Unité de traitement graphique                                |\n| Hiérarchie mémoire         | Organisation de la mémoire par vitesse et capacité           |"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ee59aabfa36af75bbbb616e4f140e53f990db0ea162b4bf86b14a788810de47f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Review Questions\n\n- What are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n- What is the role of the CPU?\n- What is the difference between a register and RAM?\n- What does the ALU do?\n- What is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n- Describe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- Why must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n- What is the purpose of cache memory?\n- How does storage differ from RAM?\n- What is a bus?\n- Why are GPUs useful?\n- Explain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n- What happens inside a computer when an application is opened?","output":"","result":"## Review Questions\n\n- What are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n- What is the role of the CPU?\n- What is the difference between a register and RAM?\n- What does the ALU do?\n- What is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n- Describe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n- Why must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n- What is the purpose of cache memory?\n- How does storage differ from RAM?\n- What is a bus?\n- Why are GPUs useful?\n- Explain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n- What happens inside a computer when an application is opened?","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-886-119a1w5-review-questions\">Review Questions</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>What are the main components of the Von Neumann architecture?\n</li>\n<li>What is the role of the CPU?\n</li>\n<li>What is the difference between a register and RAM?\n</li>\n<li>What does the ALU do?\n</li>\n<li>What is the purpose of the Control Unit?\n</li>\n<li>Describe the fetch-decode-execute cycle.\n</li>\n<li>Why must programs be loaded into RAM before execution?\n</li>\n<li>What is the purpose of cache memory?\n</li>\n<li>How does storage differ from RAM?\n</li>\n<li>What is a bus?\n</li>\n<li>Why are GPUs useful?\n</li>\n<li>Explain the memory hierarchy from registers to storage.\n</li>\n<li>What happens inside a computer when an application is opened?\n</li>\n</ul>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"7d92cbaf84db57c93decec251fed9aba1ed75c0a1f95445cab1ce867995ed483","markdown":"## Beoordelingsvragen\n\n- Wat zijn de belangrijkste componenten van de Von Neumann-architectuur?\n- Wat is de rol van de CPU?\n- Wat is het verschil tussen een register en RAM?\n- Wat doet de ALU?\n- Wat is het doel van de besturingseenheid (Control Unit)?\n- Beschrijf de fetch-decode-execute-cyclus.\n- Waarom moeten programma's in RAM geladen worden voordat ze uitgevoerd worden?\n- Wat is het doel van cachegeheugen?\n- Hoe verschilt opslag (storage) van RAM?\n- Wat is een bus?\n- Waarom zijn GPU's nuttig?\n- Leg de geheugenhierarchie uit van registers tot opslag.\n- Wat gebeurt er binnenin een computer wanneer een toepassing wordt geopend?"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"7d92cbaf84db57c93decec251fed9aba1ed75c0a1f95445cab1ce867995ed483","markdown":"## Questions de révision\n\n- Quels sont les principaux composants de l'architecture de Von Neumann ?\n- Quel est le rôle du processeur (CPU) ?\n- Quelle est la différence entre un registre et la RAM ?\n- Que fait l'UAL (ALU) ?\n- Quel est le rôle de l'unité de contrôle ?\n- Décrivez le cycle récupération-décodage-exécution.\n- Pourquoi les programmes doivent-ils être chargés en RAM avant exécution ?\n- Quel est le rôle de la mémoire cache ?\n- En quoi le stockage (mémoire de masse) diffère-t-il de la RAM ?\n- Qu'est-ce qu'un bus ?\n- Pourquoi les GPU sont-ils utiles ?\n- Expliquez la hiérarchie de la mémoire, des registres jusqu'au stockage.\n- Que se passe-t-il à l'intérieur d'un ordinateur lorsqu'une application est ouverte ?"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"7d92cbaf84db57c93decec251fed9aba1ed75c0a1f95445cab1ce867995ed483","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 5\n\nWe now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore **software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.**","output":"","result":"## Transition to Lecture 5\n\nWe now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore **software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.**","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-13g62dh-887-4rakn2-transition-to-lecture-5\">Transition to Lecture 5</h2>\n<p>We now understand how computer hardware executes instructions. But where do those instructions come from?  \nIn the next chapter, we will explore <strong>software, machine code, assembly language, and the connection between human-written programs and the hardware that executes them.</strong></p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1d9d114d121238496e0d38f1ea5d222197a6d79e652cf3d60b648887ff8e1a06","markdown":"## Overgang naar college 5\n\nWe begrijpen nu hoe computerhardware instructies uitvoert.  \nMaar waar komen die instructies vandaan?  \nIn het volgende hoofdstuk verkennen we **software, machinecode, assemblytaal, en de verbinding tussen door mensen geschreven programma's en de hardware die ze uitvoert.**"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1d9d114d121238496e0d38f1ea5d222197a6d79e652cf3d60b648887ff8e1a06","markdown":"## Transition vers la leçon 5\n\nNous comprenons maintenant comment le matériel informatique exécute des instructions. Mais d'où viennent ces instructions ?  \nDans le chapitre suivant, nous explorerons **les logiciels, le code machine, le langage d'assemblage, et le lien entre les programmes écrits par des humains et le matériel qui les exécute.**"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1d9d114d121238496e0d38f1ea5d222197a6d79e652cf3d60b648887ff8e1a06","language":"English"}}]